WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.776 --> 00:00:02.248
- Bacon?

00:00:02.248 --> 00:00:03.081
Bacon?

00:00:04.441 --> 00:00:06.086
- Hi guys, my name is
Steven Anthony Lawrence

00:00:06.086 --> 00:00:07.643
I was Beans on "Even Stevens."

00:00:07.643 --> 00:00:09.338
Everybody has a Beans in their life

00:00:09.338 --> 00:00:10.666
or they are the Beans.

00:00:10.666 --> 00:00:13.499
If you can't think of one you are. 

00:00:22.266 --> 00:00:24.059
- That's one of the top three
fake cries I've ever heard

00:00:24.059 --> 00:00:26.027
and two of them belong to me.

00:00:26.027 --> 00:00:27.209
- Thanks.

00:00:27.209 --> 00:00:28.586
I've got skills.

00:00:28.586 --> 00:00:31.710
- You know you work five
days a week with people

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:35.446
for four years and it's a set like that,

00:00:35.446 --> 00:00:39.409
you become very, very,
very, very close to people.

00:00:39.409 --> 00:00:40.575
You know, it was like a family.

00:00:40.575 --> 00:00:42.774
There was not a dry eye

00:00:42.774 --> 00:00:45.267
in the studio on the last finale.

00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:46.974
Shia has a wacky side.

00:00:46.974 --> 00:00:49.100
Maybe I like him because I kind of have

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:51.337
a wacky side too, I guess.

00:00:51.337 --> 00:00:54.695
But, you know, he has a huge heart,

00:00:54.695 --> 00:00:57.058
he'd literally give you
the shirt off of his back.

00:00:57.058 --> 00:00:58.824
I still lived in Fresno, actually,

00:00:58.824 --> 00:01:00.226
when I was shooting the show.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:02.605
My dad was driving me back and forth,

00:01:02.605 --> 00:01:05.843
you know, putting a lot of miles on cars.

00:01:05.843 --> 00:01:08.413
Shia one day just kind of
surprised me with an Xbox

00:01:08.413 --> 00:01:09.754
on Christmas.

00:01:10.209 --> 00:01:11.336
- Well from now on,

00:01:11.336 --> 00:01:13.252
your name is Beans.

00:01:15.011 --> 00:01:16.359
- Why Beans?

00:01:16.359 --> 00:01:18.596
- Kid, a nickname is not
supposed to be logical,

00:01:18.596 --> 00:01:20.209
see, it's supposed to be fun.

00:01:20.209 --> 00:01:22.377
- The audition process
was pretty cool, actually.

00:01:22.377 --> 00:01:24.749
You know, you have pre-reads

00:01:24.749 --> 00:01:26.346
and then you have your call backs.

00:01:26.346 --> 00:01:28.291
My thing, my personal
thing that I always did

00:01:28.291 --> 00:01:30.242
as an actor, as a kid at least,

00:01:30.242 --> 00:01:33.290
was I kind of feel out the room,

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:35.550
see if they were kind of in a rush or not,

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:36.807
if they were kind of connecting.

00:01:36.807 --> 00:01:38.609
Then I'd ask if they
wanted to hear a joke.

00:01:38.609 --> 00:01:40.795
So, I told this pirate joke.

00:01:40.795 --> 00:01:42.381
There was a pirate on a ship,

00:01:42.381 --> 00:01:44.704
- And the ship was a rockin' and a rollin'

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.332
and I fell off me ship.

00:01:46.332 --> 00:01:49.535
And a killer whale came
and bit off me leg.

00:01:49.535 --> 00:01:53.118
And I said to him "How'd
you get the hook?"

00:01:56.485 --> 00:01:59.192
It was the first kind of
stunt thing I had to do,

00:01:59.192 --> 00:02:01.494
they lowered me down like
"Mission: Impossible"

00:02:01.494 --> 00:02:02.888
while the girls were sleeping.

00:02:02.888 --> 00:02:05.883
It was the most jerry-rigged stunt ever.

00:02:05.883 --> 00:02:07.931
It was like one of those pulley systems.

00:02:07.931 --> 00:02:10.319
All this grip needed to do

00:02:10.319 --> 00:02:13.027
was for me to just piss him
off one day or something,

00:02:13.027 --> 00:02:15.777
and go (grunts).

00:02:27.998 --> 00:02:29.910
I am still doing classes.

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:31.950
I do only charge 40 bucks a week.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:34.330
I teach kids, I teach all ages.

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:35.681
Anybody that's hungry.

00:02:35.681 --> 00:02:38.516
I think it's a big, big, big blessing

00:02:38.516 --> 00:02:43.135
to get kids to start learning
technique at an early age

00:02:43.135 --> 00:02:46.446
instead of just making faces
in front of the camera.

00:02:46.446 --> 00:02:47.608
We underestimate kids.

00:02:47.608 --> 00:02:50.858
Kids can be pretty darn smart at times.

00:02:56.545 --> 00:02:57.795
Maybe.

00:02:57.795 --> 00:03:02.532
Maybe, I can't actually say
anything right now about that.

